@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Delete Your Account | Valour";
    ViewData["Description"] = "How to delete your Valour account and data, what is deleted, and what is kept.";
}

<div class="container legal-page">
    <div class="legal-layout">
        <partial name="_LegalNav" model="@("/delete-account/")" />

        <article class="legal-document">
            <h1>Delete Your Account</h1>
            <p>
                This page explains how to delete your account on Valour, the community chat platform operated by
                Valour Software LLC. It applies to Valour on every platform, including the Android app
                (<code>gg.valour.app</code>), the other desktop and mobile apps, and Valour on the web. One account works across all of them, so deleting it once
                removes it everywhere. You do not need the app installed to delete your account.
            </p>

            <h2 id="in-app">Delete your account in Valour</h2>
            <ol class="deletion-steps">
                <li>Sign in to the Valour app, or go to <a href="https://app.valour.gg">app.valour.gg</a> in any browser.</li>
                <li>
                    Open <strong>Settings</strong> with the gear button next to your name at the bottom of the sidebar.
                    On a phone, tap the menu button in the top left corner first to show the sidebar.
                </li>
                <li>Under <strong>General Settings</strong>, open <strong>Profile</strong> and scroll to the <strong>Account</strong> section.</li>
                <li>Select <strong>Delete Account</strong>, enter your password, and select <strong>Confirm</strong>.</li>
            </ol>

            <div class="deletion-shots">
                <figure>
                    <img src="/media/delete-account/step-1.png" alt="The Valour sidebar with the settings gear next to the username" loading="lazy" width="540" height="1170" />
                    <figcaption>Open Settings from the sidebar</figcaption>
                </figure>
                <figure>
                    <img src="/media/delete-account/step-2.png" alt="The Account section of profile settings with the Delete Account button" loading="lazy" width="540" height="1170" />
                    <figcaption>Account section in Profile</figcaption>
                </figure>
                <figure>
                    <img src="/media/delete-account/step-3.png" alt="The Delete Account confirmation asking for your password" loading="lazy" width="540" height="1170" />
                    <figcaption>Confirm with your password</figcaption>
                </figure>
            </div>

            <p class="deletion-callout">
                Deletion happens immediately and cannot be undone. You are signed out on every device, and there is
                no waiting period in which the account can be restored.
            </p>

            <h2 id="by-email">If you cannot sign in</h2>
            <p>
                If you have forgotten your password, you can reset it from the
                <a href="https://app.valour.gg/ForgotPassword">password recovery page</a> and then follow the steps above.
            </p>
            <p>
                Otherwise, email <a href="mailto:support@valour.gg?subject=Delete%20my%20account">support@valour.gg</a>
                from the email address registered to your account, with the subject "Delete my account" and your
                username. We may ask you to confirm that you own the account. We complete verified requests within
                30 days and reply when the account has been deleted.
            </p>

            <h2 id="deleted">What is deleted</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Your account details: email address, password, date of birth, two-factor authentication, and sign-in sessions.</li>
                <li>Your profile, avatar, profile background and preferences.</li>
                <li>Every message you sent, in any channel, with its reactions, mentions and attachments.</li>
                <li>Your direct message conversations. Both sides of a one-to-one conversation are removed.</li>
                <li>Files you uploaded, removed from storage once nothing else uses them.</li>
                <li>Threads you started, including all comments on them. Comments you left on other people's threads are replaced with an empty "deleted" placeholder so replies keep their place.</li>
                <li>Your friends, friend requests, blocks, planet and group chat memberships, planet bans, and invites you created.</li>
                <li>Encrypted key backups, linked devices and pending key requests used for end-to-end encryption.</li>
                <li>Notifications, push notification registrations, calendar RSVPs, activity statistics, planet folders, GIF favorites and referrals.</li>
                <li>Economy accounts, balances, items and transaction history.</li>
                <li>Bots and OAuth applications you own.</li>
                <li>Your Stargazer subscription, which is cancelled with no further charges. The billing customer record held by our payment processor, Stripe, is also deleted.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 id="kept">What is kept, and why</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <strong>Planets you own.</strong> Planets belong to their communities, so they are not deleted.
                    Ownership moves to Valour's system account. To hand a planet to someone else, transfer ownership
                    in the planet's settings before you delete your account.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Shared planet content.</strong> Wiki pages, calendar events, webhooks and themes you
                    published stay available to their communities. They are credited to Valour's system account
                    and are no longer linked to you.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Your public encryption keys.</strong> The log of public keys for your account is kept so
                    other people can still verify messages in shared conversations. It holds public keys only and
                    cannot decrypt anything.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Safety and moderation records.</strong> Reports about your account and moderation logs
                    are kept with the link to your account removed. Files flagged by child-safety checks are preserved
                    when the law requires it.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Records we are legally required to keep.</strong> Data covered by a legal hold or a valid
                    legal obligation is kept only for as long as that obligation lasts. Stripe keeps its own records
                    of past payments as payment regulations require.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                If you joined planets hosted on independently operated community nodes, Valour tells those nodes to
                delete their copy of your account.
            </p>

            <h2 id="partial">Delete some data without deleting your account</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Messages:</strong> delete any message you sent from its message menu.</li>
                <li><strong>Files:</strong> open Settings, then <strong>Attachments</strong>, to find and delete files you uploaded.</li>
                <li><strong>Threads and comments:</strong> delete them from their menus in the planet's thread feed.</li>
                <li><strong>Friends, blocks and sessions:</strong> manage them from the Friends, Safety and Security pages in Settings.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                For any other request, email <a href="mailto:support@valour.gg">support@valour.gg</a>. Our
                <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> describes all of the data we collect and your rights.
            </p>
        </article>
    </div>
</div>
